# Said "expected an expression", caret on the `:=`. The one identifier position
# that does NOT route through `eat`: every binding branch of `parse_stmt` gates on
# TK_IDENT, so a keyword falls through to the expression parser. Its own arm.
# expect: 'spawn' is a reserved keyword and cannot be used as a variable name
fn main():
    spawn := 1
    println(str(spawn))
